// The agent pane's and command palette's icons. The dark palette's files bake
// in a colour drawn for a dark ground (#DDDDDD-#FAFAFA, #919191, indigo.200),
// which all but vanishes on this palette's light ones, so each `*_white.svg`
// beside it is the same drawing recoloured:
//
//   * near-white ink -> #353430, `icon/primary/default`'s Light value
//     (clay.900), which is also the ink of the secondary and tertiary buttons
//     most of these sit on;
//   * the #919191 tier (`icon/primary/subtle` in the dark mode) -> #7a756a,
//     clay.700. The subtle token's own Light value, clay.550, is 2.9:1 on this
//     palette's input ground, under the 3:1 WCAG 1.4.11 asks of an icon;
//     clay.700 is the light caption tier the gutter numbers already use;
//   * the AI avatar's indigo.200 -> indigo.500, the brand colour both
//     palettes already use for CT_PRIMARY_DEFAULT and TRACEPOINT_COLOR;
//   * the permission dot's red.400 -> red.600, `icon/error/primary`'s Light
//     value, as its label next to it takes the error text token here.
//
// Two keep the dark theme's file on purpose. The send button's white glyph
// sits on the primary action surface, whose content colour in this mode is
// `text/on-action-primary`, grey.50 — near-white is the design system's own
// choice there. The stop button's #DDDDDD glyph sits on red.700 in both
// themes.
